  "temperature": "Temperature",
  "@temperature": {
    "description": "AI sampling temperature: rescales legal-move logits before softmax; not physical device temperature. At zero Maia selects an argmax. Use the same localized term in help, value announcements and HTML reports. Official localized AI terminology sources: docs/TRANSLATION_QUALITY_REVIEW.md."
  },
  "topP": "Top-P",
  "@topP": {
    "description": "Top-P (nucleus sampling): retain the smallest highest-probability candidate set whose cumulative probability reaches P, including the crossing move. Keep the conventional Top-P identifier. Not a per-move percentage cutoff. Official AI terminology sources: docs/TRANSLATION_QUALITY_REVIEW.md."
  },
  "maxOpeningVariety": "Max variety in opening",
  "@maxOpeningVariety": {
    "description": "Settings: maximize opening variety for the first five moves by each side"
  },
  "maxOpeningVarietyHelp": "On by default. Uses Temperature and Top-P 1.0 / 1.0 for the first five moves by each side, then your configured settings from move 6. This keeps broad opening choices while allowing you to trim low-probability moves later. It follows the position’s move number, including when resuming or continuing a game.\n\nNot needed at 1.0 / 1.0: the switch is off and unavailable because those settings already give full variety throughout.",
  "@maxOpeningVarietyHelp": {
    "description": "Maia-specific sampling guidance for the 2.5 default proposal. Preserve probability mass versus individual move probability, the five-full-move boundary and conditional direct-match strength claims. Not a Lichess equivalent. Explanation selector changes prose only."
  },
